{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And cassia.</b> A name for the root of an herb; in the language of the Sages — קְצִיעָה." "<b>A hin.</b> Twelve log; and the Sages of Israel disagreed concerning it — Rabbi Meir says: in it they boiled the roots. Rabbi Yehudah said to him: But to anoint with the roots — it is not a substitute; rather, they soaked them in the water so that they would not absorb the oil, and afterwards he floated the oil over them until it absorbed the fragrance, and he skimmed off the oil from over the roots (Horayot 11)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:49.487210673Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}